<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_RakatanCommandCodes - ASHFALL_RESEARCH_BASE_1's whole reason to exist:
  the physical MacGuffin that opens ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1's shielding.

  Ruled verbatim (ashfall_research_base.md §6, plot sitting 2026-09-12,
  restated in full at the_propane_lakes.md §8's amendment): "The command
  codes CANNOT be granted by the cathedral. They are on an isolated system
  within the command center (dark spire) and were never ceeded to the
  cathedral" => "the Rakatan command codes are the only way into the ancient
  war lab... once it's revealed by the melting event." This is a TWO-KEY
  dungeon: the crater event (WAR_LAB_CRATER_HOOK_1) opens the GROUND; this
  item opens the DOOR.

  Modeled on vanilla AIPersonaCore/TechprofSubpersonaCore (Core,
  Items_Exotic.xml) - ResourceBase + ThingWithComps, a stack-1 haulable data
  core, not a building: it must physically travel from the Spire (Ashfall
  Range, dayside) to the war lab (propane lake, antipodal night side), which
  a claimable-building precedent (RUT_WarLabArchive/RUT_SpireCommandConsole)
  cannot do.

  tradeability=None (not Sellable): this is a plot key, not loot - a crew
  that pawns it off mid-campaign should not be able to un-softlock itself by
  buying a replacement, and there is only ever one.

  CompRedeemRakatanCommandCodes (Source/Ashfall/CompRedeemRakatanCommandCodes.cs)
  is the "quest-item/quest-flag mechanism" ASHFALL_RESEARCH_BASE_1.md's own
  filing note asks for: a gizmo that calls AshfallCommandCodesFlag.Seize()
  (GameComponent_AshfallCommandCodes, permanent/idempotent, same discipline
  as WarLabCraterMutation/GameComponent_WarLabCrater) and consumes the item -
  the in-fiction reading is "keying the codes into a lock", ready for
  whichever item finishes the war lab's own door to gate on
  AshfallCommandCodesFlag.HasBeenSeized instead of re-deriving this from
  scratch.

  NOT RESOLVED THIS PASS (flagged, not guessed): whether redeeming should be
  restricted to only the war lab's own map/site. That restriction needs the
  war lab's own map/site identity, which belongs to whichever item wires the
  actual door check (ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1/WAR_LAB_CRATER_HOOK_1's own scope, see
  ASHFALL_RESEARCH_BASE_1.md's "Watch out"). This pass's gizmo is usable
  anywhere, which is deliberately over-permissive rather than under-built: a
  flag that CAN be set from the wrong place is a design cleanup later; a flag
  that CANNOT be set at all is a dead mechanism now. Also unresolved:
  whether simple possession (not redemption) should be enough for the door
  check instead of the flag - either reading is defensible and left to that
  item to decide.

  Art: reuses Things/Item/Special/SubpersonaCoreTechprof (Core,
  Items_Exotic.xml) - a small AI-core-like data device art already ships
  with the game; no new art authored this pass.
-->
<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_RakatanCommandCodes</defName>
    <label>Rakatan command codes</label>
    <description>A data-core seized from an isolated system deep in the Spire — Rakatan military cryptography, never ceded to any cathedral, never meant to leave this room. Whatever it unlocks, it was built to unlock only once.</description>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/SubpersonaCoreTechprof</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
    <soundInteract>Metal_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Metal_Drop</soundDrop>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>1</MarketValue>
      <MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints>
      <Mass>1.5</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ItemsMisc</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <drawGUIOverlay>false</drawGUIOverlay>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <techLevel>Archotech</techLevel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.StructureInjectionsRUT.CompProperties_RedeemRakatanCommandCodes" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>
</Defs>
